    "body": "## Summary\n\n`multi_json` deprecated `encode`/`decode` (and the `MultiJson` constant) in [1.21.0](https://github.com/sferik/multi_json/blob/v1.21.1/CHANGELOG.md) and plans to remove them in 2.0.0. neovim-ruby's only production use is the JSON log formatter in `lib/neovim/logging.rb`, so this replaces it with the standard library `JSON` and drops the dependency entirely.\n\n## Changes\n\n- `lib/neovim/logging.rb`: `MultiJson.encode` → `JSON.generate`\n- `neovim.gemspec`: remove `add_dependency \"multi_json\", \"~> 1.0\"`\n- `spec/neovim/logging_spec.rb`: `MultiJson.decode` → `JSON.parse`\n\n`JSON.generate` produces output equivalent to `MultiJson.encode` for the symbol-keyed hash used here, and the return value is still a `String`, so the trailing `<< \"\\n\"` is unchanged. `json` is part of the standard library, so no new dependency is introduced.\n\n## Testing\n\n- `bundle exec rspec` — all green\n- The single pre-existing acceptance failure (`Client info get_client_info`) reproduces on a clean checkout and is unrelated to this change.\n\n## Alternative\n\nIf you'd prefer to keep `multi_json`, the minimal forward-compatible change is to use the renamed API (`MultiJSON.generate`) and bump the dependency to `>= 1.21`. Happy to switch to that approach if you'd rather keep the abstraction.\n",
    "closed_at": "2026-06-30T01:03:40Z",
